WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
And to wrap things up, you have finished the course, you now have a pretty complete foundation for what you need to continue on your Python journey no matter what your passion is.

00:13.000 --> 00:19.000
Next steps, if you want to stay in touch, if you enjoyed the course, I would love to hear from you.

00:19.000 --> 00:24.000
I'm most active on Twitter, sometimes I blog, sometimes I stream on Twitch.

00:24.000 --> 00:30.000
But you can follow me on Twitter at NNJA or watch my other courses on Frontend Masters.

00:30.000 --> 00:34.000
And I have a bunch of links for you here for continuing your journey.

00:34.000 --> 00:43.000
The basics, some more links about web development and Django, some information about AI and machine learning and data processing.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.000
But most importantly, I think, is the Python community.

00:47.000 --> 00:51.000
There are lots of local user groups worldwide that are listed in the wiki.

00:51.000 --> 00:56.000
There's a Python discord with 100,000 developers on it.

00:56.000 --> 01:02.000
There are tons of support of groups out there for women and non-binary developers, like I mentioned earlier,

01:02.000 --> 01:07.000
Pilates and Django girls, and the Python community would love to have you.

01:07.000 --> 01:11.000
So, congratulations for finishing Practical Python.

01:11.000 --> 01:14.000
Feel free to give yourselves a round of applause.

01:14.000 --> 01:19.000
You all did a great job, and I hope that you continue your Python journey.

01:20.000 --> 01:24.000
Are there any questions?

01:24.000 --> 01:29.000
Oh, no. Someone in chat just went.

01:29.000 --> 01:33.000
This course was head exploding.

01:33.000 --> 01:35.000
Yeah, you all learned a lot.

01:35.000 --> 01:39.000
You really, I think, have a lot of the foundational knowledge.

01:39.000 --> 01:42.000
You need to write Python apps, or most importantly, read them.

01:42.000 --> 01:47.000
You know about the tools and the skills that you need to work on Python projects successfully on a team.

01:47.000 --> 01:52.000
So, you have it all, and I hope to see you succeed.

01:52.000 --> 01:55.000
I hope to read some of your Python programs one day.

